Write a function `separate_string_number/1` that takes a string and returns a list of its alphanumeric components. Letters form separate string elements, while numeric sequences become integer or float elements. A numeric sequence containing a period (`.`) must be interpreted as a float; otherwise, it is an integer. The function must preserve the order of the components and handle all inputs, including empty strings, by returning an empty list.

